1
00:00:01,500 --> 00:00:03,800
You are the weakest link.

2
00:00:05,900 --> 00:00:10,400
This isn't just a game.
There's something else going on.

3
00:00:10,400 --> 00:00:13,500
We have contestants outside
the games. The games continue.

4
00:00:13,500 --> 00:00:15,300
This is Satellite Five.

5
00:00:15,400 --> 00:00:18,200
10, 000 channels,
all beaming down from here.

6
00:00:18,200 --> 00:00:19,800
My masters fear the Doctor.

7
00:00:19,900 --> 00:00:24,100
Tell me, who they are? !
You're dead, I saw you die!

8
00:00:24,200 --> 00:00:27,700
That's impossible, they were
destroyed. Obviously they survived.

9
00:00:27,700 --> 00:00:33,600
We have your associate. You will
obey or she will be exterminated.

10
00:00:33,600 --> 00:00:35,100
- Rose?
- Yes, Doctor?

11
00:00:35,200 --> 00:00:36,600
I'm coming to get you.

12
00:01:14,600 --> 00:01:17,400
You know the Doctor.

13
00:01:17,400 --> 00:01:21,100
You understand him.
You will predict his actions.

14
00:01:21,200 --> 00:01:24,400
I don't know! Even if I did,
I wouldn't tell you.

15
00:01:24,500 --> 00:01:26,700
Predict! Predict! Predict!

16
00:01:26,700 --> 00:01:29,200
Tardis detected in flight.

17
00:01:29,300 --> 00:01:32,800
Launch missiles! Exterminate!

18
00:01:32,900 --> 00:01:35,700
You can't! The Tardis has
no defences, you'll kill him!

19
00:01:35,800 --> 00:01:39,200
You have predicted correctly.

20
00:01:42,600 --> 00:01:44,200
We got incoming!

21
00:01:52,500 --> 00:01:58,100
The extrapolator's working, we've
got a fully-functional force field.
Try saying that when you're drunk.

22
00:01:58,200 --> 00:01:59,900
And for my next trick. . .

23
00:02:22,800 --> 00:02:24,800
Rose, get down!

24
00:02:25,500 --> 00:02:28,400
Get down, Rose! Exterminate!

25
00:02:29,700 --> 00:02:31,900
Aaaah!

26
00:02:34,500 --> 00:02:36,700
You did it.

27
00:02:40,200 --> 00:02:43,100
It feels like I haven't
seen you in years!

28
00:02:43,200 --> 00:02:47,700
I told you I'd come and get you.
I never doubted it. I did.
You all right? Yeah, you?

29
00:02:47,700 --> 00:02:52,700
Not bad, been better. Hey,
don't I get a hug? Oh, come here!
I was talking to him.

30
00:02:52,700 --> 00:02:56,300
Welcome home. Oh. . .
I thought I'd never see you again.

31
00:02:56,300 --> 00:03:01,900
You were lucky, that was a one-shot
wonder. It drained the gun of its
power supply, now it's just junk.

32
00:03:03,700 --> 00:03:06,900
Patience, my brethren. . .

33
00:03:06,900 --> 00:03:09,300
You said they were extinct.

34
00:03:09,300 --> 00:03:13,600
One minute they're
the greatest threat in the universe,
then they vanish.

35
00:03:13,600 --> 00:03:16,400
They went off to fight a bigger war.

36
00:03:16,500 --> 00:03:18,500
The Time War.

37
00:03:18,500 --> 00:03:21,500
I thought that was just a legend.
I was there,

38
00:03:21,600 --> 00:03:26,100
the war between the Daleks
and the Time Lords,
with the whole of creation at stake.

39
00:03:26,100 --> 00:03:29,200
My people were destroyed,
but took the Daleks with them.

40
00:03:29,200 --> 00:03:32,300
I almost thought it was worth it,

41
00:03:32,400 --> 00:03:35,300
and now it turns out
they died for nothing.

42
00:03:35,300 --> 00:03:38,800
There's thousands of them now,
we could hardly stop one.

43
00:03:38,800 --> 00:03:40,900
What are we gonna do?

44
00:03:41,000 --> 00:03:43,300
No good stood round here
chin-wagging.

45
00:03:43,300 --> 00:03:45,100
Human Race, you'd gossip all day.

46
00:03:45,100 --> 00:03:51,100
The Daleks have got the answers,
let's go and meet the neighbours.
You can't go out there!

47
00:03:51,100 --> 00:03:53,700
Exterminate! Exterminate!

48
00:03:57,800 --> 00:03:59,600
Is that it?

49
00:03:59,600 --> 00:04:03,100
Useless! Nul points!

50
00:04:03,100 --> 00:04:07,600
It's all right, come on out, that
force field can hold back anything.
Almost anything.

51
00:04:07,700 --> 00:04:11,700
Yes, but I wasn't going to tell them
that, thanks. Sorry.

52
00:04:14,500 --> 00:04:18,600
Do you know what they call me
in the ancient legends
of the Dalek homeworld?

53
00:04:18,600 --> 00:04:20,600
The Oncoming Storm.

54
00:04:20,600 --> 00:04:25,100
You might have removed all your
emotions, but I reckon, right down

55
00:04:25,100 --> 00:04:29,300
deep in your DNA,
there's one little spark left.

56
00:04:29,400 --> 00:04:30,600
And that's fear.

57
00:04:33,100 --> 00:04:36,000
Doesn't it just burn
when you face me?

58
00:04:36,000 --> 00:04:38,400
So tell me. . .

59
00:04:38,400 --> 00:04:41,600
how did you survive the Time War?

60
00:04:41,600 --> 00:04:44,900
They survived through me.

61
00:04:57,700 --> 00:05:00,800
Rose, Captain. . .

62
00:05:02,300 --> 00:05:04,400
.this is the Emperor of the Daleks.

63
00:05:04,500 --> 00:05:07,000
You destroyed us, Doctor.

64
00:05:07,100 --> 00:05:11,200
The Dalek race died in your inferno,

65
00:05:11,300 --> 00:05:13,700
but my ship survived,

66
00:05:13,700 --> 00:05:18,400
falling through time,
crippled but alive.

67
00:05:18,400 --> 00:05:20,400
I get it. Do not interrupt!

68
00:05:20,400 --> 00:05:23,800
Do not interrupt! Do not interrupt!

69
00:05:23,800 --> 00:05:29,100
I think you're forgetting something.
I'm the Doctor, and if there's
one thing I can do, it's talk.

70
00:05:29,200 --> 00:05:32,600
I've got five billion languages
and you've no way of stopping me,

71
00:05:32,600 --> 00:05:34,900
so if anybody's gonna shut up,
it's you!

72
00:05:36,400 --> 00:05:38,900
Okey-doke! So. . .where were we?

73
00:05:38,900 --> 00:05:43,500
We waited here in the dark space,

74
00:05:43,500 --> 00:05:47,200
damaged but rebuilding.

75
00:05:47,300 --> 00:05:54,400
Centuries passed, and we quietly
infiltrated the systems of Earth,

76
00:05:54,400 --> 00:05:57,800
harvesting the waste of humanity.

77
00:05:57,900 --> 00:06:04,100
The prisoners, the refugees, the
dispossessed, they all came to us.

78
00:06:04,100 --> 00:06:08,400
The bodies were filleted,
pulped, sifted.

79
00:06:08,400 --> 00:06:11,600
The seed of the human race
is perverted.

80
00:06:11,600 --> 00:06:15,900
Only one cell in a billion
was fit to be nurtured.

81
00:06:16,000 --> 00:06:19,300
So you created an army
of Daleks out of the dead.

82
00:06:19,400 --> 00:06:22,600
That makes them. . .half human.

83
00:06:22,600 --> 00:06:24,100
Those words are blasphemy!

84
00:06:26,300 --> 00:06:28,100
Do not blaspheme!

85
00:06:28,100 --> 00:06:31,300
Do not blaspheme! Do not blaspheme!

86
00:06:31,300 --> 00:06:35,200
Everything human has been purged.

87
00:06:35,200 --> 00:06:40,700
I cultivated pure and blessed Dalek.

88
00:06:44,100 --> 00:06:47,400
Since when did the Daleks
have a concept of blasphemy?

89
00:06:47,400 --> 00:06:52,300
I reached into the dirt
and made new life.

90
00:06:52,300 --> 00:06:56,000
I am the god of all Daleks!

91
00:06:56,000 --> 00:06:57,700
Worship him!

92
00:06:57,800 --> 00:07:00,100
Worship him! Worship him!

93
00:07:00,100 --> 00:07:02,900
They're insane.

94
00:07:02,900 --> 00:07:06,900
Hiding in silence for hundreds of
years is enough to drive anyone mad,

95
00:07:06,900 --> 00:07:09,100
but it's worse than that.

96
00:07:09,100 --> 00:07:13,400
Driven mad by your own flesh. . .

97
00:07:14,600 --> 00:07:17,000
The stink of humanity.

98
00:07:20,300 --> 00:07:22,800
You hate your own existence.

99
00:07:25,100 --> 00:07:27,700
And that makes them
more deadly than ever.

100
00:07:29,700 --> 00:07:33,800
We're going.
You may not leave my presence!

101
00:07:33,800 --> 00:07:35,800
Stay where you are!

102
00:07:35,900 --> 00:07:39,000
Exterminate! Exterminate!

103
00:07:39,000 --> 00:07:40,900
Exterminate!

104
00:07:40,900 --> 00:07:43,500
Exterminate! Exterminate!

105
00:07:43,500 --> 00:07:45,000
Exterminate!

106
00:07:45,100 --> 00:07:48,500
Worship him! Worship him!

107
00:07:48,600 --> 00:07:50,000
Exterminate! Exterminate!

108
00:07:59,900 --> 00:08:05,400
Turn everything up,
all transmitters, full power, wide
open, now! Do it! What does this do?

109
00:08:05,400 --> 00:08:10,500
Stops Daleks transmatting on board.
Did you contact Earth? I tried to,
but they suspended our licence

110
00:08:10,500 --> 00:08:14,700
cos we stopped the programmes.
Then the planet's defenceless.

111
00:08:14,800 --> 00:08:17,600
Lynda, what are you
still doing on board?

112
00:08:17,600 --> 00:08:19,600
I told you to evacuate everyone!

113
00:08:19,700 --> 00:08:22,400
She wouldn't go.
I didn't wanna leave you.

114
00:08:22,500 --> 00:08:26,000
There weren't enough shuttles anyway
or I wouldn't be here.

115
00:08:26,000 --> 00:08:28,400
We've got 100 people stranded
on Floor Zero.

116
00:08:28,400 --> 00:08:31,000
Listen, listen, my name's Rodrick.

117
00:08:31,000 --> 00:08:35,700
I won the game, where's my money? Is
anyone listening? Where's my money?

118
00:08:35,700 --> 00:08:37,500
Oh, my God, the Fleet is moving.

119
00:08:37,500 --> 00:08:39,400
They're on their way.

120
00:08:44,300 --> 00:08:47,200
Purify the Earth with fire.

121
00:08:47,200 --> 00:08:52,700
The planet will become my temple
and we shall rise.

122
00:08:52,700 --> 00:08:57,600
This will be our paradise.

123
00:09:04,400 --> 00:09:08,300
Dalek plan, big mistake, cos what
have they left me with? Anyone?

124
00:09:08,300 --> 00:09:13,100
Oh, come on, it's obvious! A
great big transmitter, this station!

125
00:09:13,200 --> 00:09:16,000
If I can change the signal,
sequence it? Anyone?

126
00:09:16,000 --> 00:09:19,200
You gotta be kidding. Give the man
a medal! A delta wave?

127
00:09:19,200 --> 00:09:21,700
A delta wave! What's a delta wave?

128
00:09:21,700 --> 00:09:24,300
Van Cassadyne energy,
it fries your brain.

129
00:09:24,400 --> 00:09:27,300
Stand in its way
and your head gets barbecued!

130
00:09:27,300 --> 00:09:32,500
And this place can transmit a
massive wave, wipe out the Daleks!
Get started and do it, then!

131
00:09:32,500 --> 00:09:37,500
But a wave this size, building
this big, brain as clever as mine,
should take. . .three days?

132
00:09:37,500 --> 00:09:39,900
How long till the fleet arrive?
22 minutes.

133
00:09:52,500 --> 00:09:58,300
With our force field, they can't
blast us out of the sky, but that
doesn't stop the Daleks invading.

134
00:09:58,400 --> 00:10:01,400
Do they know about the delta wave?
They'll have worked it out.

135
00:10:01,400 --> 00:10:05,400
They wanna stop the Doctor,
so they've got to get to level 500.

136
00:10:05,500 --> 00:10:09,600
I can concentrate the extrapolator
on the top six levels, 500 to 495,

137
00:10:09,700 --> 00:10:14,700
so they'll penetrate the station
below that, at level 494,
and fight their way up.

138
00:10:14,700 --> 00:10:17,400
Who are they fighting? Us.
And what are we fighting with?

139
00:10:17,400 --> 00:10:22,000
The guards had guns with bastic
bullets, enough to blow a Dalek
wide open. There's five of us.

140
00:10:22,100 --> 00:10:25,400
Rose, you can help me, I need
all these wires stripping bare.

141
00:10:25,500 --> 00:10:27,000
Right, now there's four of us.

142
00:10:27,100 --> 00:10:31,100
Then let's move it! Into the lift,
isolate the lift controls.

143
00:10:33,800 --> 00:10:37,400
I-I just wanna say, um. . .thanks,

144
00:10:37,500 --> 00:10:40,500
I suppose. And I'll do my best.

145
00:10:40,500 --> 00:10:42,400
Me too.

146
00:10:55,600 --> 00:10:56,700
It's been fun.

147
00:10:58,300 --> 00:11:00,400
But I guess this is goodbye.

148
00:11:00,500 --> 00:11:04,700
Don't talk like that, the Doctor's
gonna do it, you just watch him.

149
00:11:04,800 --> 00:11:06,200
Rose. . .

150
00:11:08,800 --> 00:11:10,900
You are worth fighting for.

151
00:11:15,300 --> 00:11:18,200
I wish I'd never met you, Doctor.

152
00:11:18,200 --> 00:11:20,800
I was much better off as a coward.

153
00:11:26,100 --> 00:11:28,500
See you in hell.

154
00:11:30,400 --> 00:11:32,500
He's gonna be all right.

155
00:11:33,900 --> 00:11:35,500
Isn't he?

156
00:11:45,600 --> 00:11:47,800
One last time!

157
00:11:47,800 --> 00:11:50,100
Any more volunteers?

158
00:11:53,500 --> 00:11:57,700
There's an army
about to invade this station.

159
00:11:57,800 --> 00:12:00,100
I need every last citizen
to mount a defence.

160
00:12:00,200 --> 00:12:02,200
Don't listen to him!

161
00:12:02,200 --> 00:12:06,100
There aren't any Daleks, they
disappeared thousands of years ago!

162
00:12:08,000 --> 00:12:09,800
Thanks.

163
00:12:09,900 --> 00:12:14,300
As for the rest of you, the Daleks
will enter the station at Floor 494,

164
00:12:14,400 --> 00:12:18,100
and as far as I can tell,
they'll head up, not down.

165
00:12:18,100 --> 00:12:20,000
But that's not a promise,

166
00:12:20,100 --> 00:12:23,400
so here's a few words of advice.

167
00:12:23,400 --> 00:12:25,300
Keep quiet.

168
00:12:25,300 --> 00:12:29,600
And if you hear fighting up above,
if you hear us dying. . .

169
00:12:29,700 --> 00:12:34,400
then tell me
that the Daleks aren't real.

170
00:12:38,900 --> 00:12:41,200
Don't make a sound.

171
00:12:41,300 --> 00:12:42,700
Let's go.

172
00:12:57,000 --> 00:12:58,900
Suppose. . .

173
00:13:02,100 --> 00:13:03,800
What?

174
00:13:03,800 --> 00:13:06,200
Nothing.

175
00:13:06,200 --> 00:13:09,200
You said, "Suppose. . ."
No, I was just thinking. . .

176
00:13:09,200 --> 00:13:11,800
and I mean, obviously,
you can't but. . .

177
00:13:11,900 --> 00:13:16,200
you've got a time machine. Why not
go back to last week and warn them?

178
00:13:16,200 --> 00:13:21,000
As soon as the Tardis lands,
in that second, I become part
of events, stuck in the timeline.

179
00:13:21,100 --> 00:13:24,200
Yeah, I thought it'd be
something like that.

180
00:13:24,300 --> 00:13:28,700
There's another thing the Tardis
could do. It could take us away.

181
00:13:28,700 --> 00:13:30,600
We could leave.

182
00:13:30,600 --> 00:13:32,500
Let history take its course.

183
00:13:32,500 --> 00:13:34,600
We go to Marbella in 1989.

184
00:13:34,700 --> 00:13:36,400
Yeah, but you'd never do that.

185
00:13:36,400 --> 00:13:38,000
No, but you could ask.

186
00:13:39,600 --> 00:13:45,600
It never even occurred to you,
did it? Well. . .I'm just too good.

187
00:13:47,700 --> 00:13:52,000
The delta wave's started building.
How long does it need?

188
00:13:59,500 --> 00:14:01,400
Is that bad?

189
00:14:01,400 --> 00:14:04,000
OK, it's bad. How bad is it?

190
00:14:05,800 --> 00:14:07,500
Rose Tyler, you're a genius!

191
00:14:07,500 --> 00:14:11,400
We can do it! If I use the Tardis
to cross my own timeline. . .

192
00:14:11,500 --> 00:14:13,000
Yes!

193
00:14:18,300 --> 00:14:21,800
Hold that down and keep position.
What's it do?

194
00:14:21,900 --> 00:14:27,300
Cancels the buffers. If I'm -
and I'm I'm brilliant - I might
just save the world or rip it apart.

195
00:14:27,300 --> 00:14:32,100
I'd go for the first one.
Me too! I've just got to power up
the Game Station, hold on!

196
00:14:54,800 --> 00:14:57,400
Doctor, what are you doing? !

197
00:14:57,400 --> 00:14:59,700
Can I take my hand off? It's moving!

198
00:15:03,000 --> 00:15:05,200
Doctor, let me out!

199
00:15:05,300 --> 00:15:07,300
Let me out!

200
00:15:07,300 --> 00:15:09,800
Doctor, let me out!

201
00:15:27,400 --> 00:15:29,300
This is Emergency Programme One.

202
00:15:29,300 --> 00:15:32,100
Rose, now listen, this is important.

203
00:15:32,100 --> 00:15:35,600
If this message has activated,
then it can only mean one thing.

204
00:15:35,700 --> 00:15:38,700
We must be in danger,
and I mean fatal.

205
00:15:38,700 --> 00:15:42,300
I'm dead or about to die at any
second with no chance of escape.

206
00:15:42,300 --> 00:15:44,500
No! And that's OK,
hope it's a good death.

207
00:15:44,500 --> 00:15:48,700
But I promised to look after you,
so the Tardis is taking you home.

208
00:15:48,700 --> 00:15:52,500
I won't let you! And I bet you're
fussing and moaning now, typical!

209
00:15:52,600 --> 00:15:54,600
But hold on
and just listen a bit more.

210
00:15:54,600 --> 00:15:56,600
The Tardis can never return for me.

211
00:15:56,600 --> 00:16:01,400
Emergency Programme One means
I'm facing an enemy that should
never get this machine.

212
00:16:01,500 --> 00:16:03,600
So this is what you do should do,

213
00:16:03,600 --> 00:16:05,600
let the Tardis die.

214
00:16:05,600 --> 00:16:07,800
Just let this old box gather dust.

215
00:16:07,900 --> 00:16:10,400
No-one can open it,
no-one'll even notice it.

216
00:16:10,500 --> 00:16:14,000
Let it become a strange little
thing standing on a street corner.

217
00:16:14,000 --> 00:16:17,300
Over the years the world will
move on and the box will be buried.

218
00:16:17,300 --> 00:16:20,200
And if you want to remember me,
then you can do one thing.

219
00:16:20,200 --> 00:16:22,200
That's all, one thing.

220
00:16:25,300 --> 00:16:27,100
Have a good life.

221
00:16:29,000 --> 00:16:31,600
Do that for me, Rose.

222
00:16:31,600 --> 00:16:34,100
Have a fantastic life.

223
00:16:39,400 --> 00:16:42,900
You can't do this to me. You can't!

224
00:16:43,000 --> 00:16:45,600
Take me back! Take me back!

225
00:16:48,700 --> 00:16:50,200
No!

226
00:17:06,200 --> 00:17:07,800
Come on, fly!

227
00:17:07,900 --> 00:17:10,500
How do you fly? !

228
00:17:10,500 --> 00:17:12,000
Come on, help me!

229
00:17:28,400 --> 00:17:30,300
I knew it!

230
00:17:30,300 --> 00:17:33,300
I was down Clifton Parade
and I heard the engines.

231
00:17:33,300 --> 00:17:36,800
I thought, "There's only one thing
that makes a noise like that."

232
00:17:36,900 --> 00:17:39,100
What is it?

233
00:17:44,500 --> 00:17:48,700
Rose, I've called up
the internal laser codes,

234
00:17:48,700 --> 00:17:54,400
there should be a different number
on every screen. Read them to me.
She's not here. Taking a leak?!

235
00:17:54,500 --> 00:17:59,100
When she gets back, tell her to read
me the codes. She's not coming back.
Where'd she go?

236
00:17:59,200 --> 00:18:01,400
Just get on with your work.

237
00:18:01,500 --> 00:18:03,700
You took her home, didn't you? Yeah.

238
00:18:05,400 --> 00:18:07,900
The delta wave,
is it ever gonna be ready?

239
00:18:08,000 --> 00:18:11,400
Tell him the truth,
Doctor.

240
00:18:11,400 --> 00:18:17,100
There is every possibility
the delta wave could be complete,

241
00:18:17,200 --> 00:18:21,100
but no possibility of refining it.

242
00:18:21,100 --> 00:18:26,200
The delta wave must kill
every living thing in its path,

243
00:18:26,300 --> 00:18:29,300
with no distinction
between human and Dalek.

244
00:18:31,200 --> 00:18:34,000
All things will die

245
00:18:34,000 --> 00:18:36,800
by your hand.

246
00:18:36,800 --> 00:18:41,400
Doctor, the range of this
transmitter covers the whole Earth.

247
00:18:41,400 --> 00:18:47,000
You would destroy
Daleks and humans together.

248
00:18:47,000 --> 00:18:49,800
If I am God,

249
00:18:49,900 --> 00:18:52,300
the creator of all things,

250
00:18:52,300 --> 00:18:56,300
then what does that
make you, Doctor?

251
00:18:56,300 --> 00:18:58,100
There are colonies out there.

252
00:18:58,100 --> 00:19:03,200
The human race would survive in
some shape or form, but you're
the only Daleks in existence.

253
00:19:03,200 --> 00:19:06,500
The whole universe is in danger
if I let you live.

254
00:19:06,600 --> 00:19:09,100
Do you see, Jack?

255
00:19:10,400 --> 00:19:14,400
That's the decision I've got
to make for every living thing.

256
00:19:14,400 --> 00:19:16,400
Die as a human or live as a Dalek.

257
00:19:16,500 --> 00:19:19,200
What would you do?

258
00:19:19,300 --> 00:19:21,100
You sent her home.

259
00:19:21,100 --> 00:19:22,500
She's safe.

260
00:19:22,600 --> 00:19:26,700
Keep working.
But he will exterminate you!

261
00:19:26,800 --> 00:19:29,300
Never doubted him, never will.

262
00:19:29,300 --> 00:19:36,300
Now you tell me, God of all Daleks,
cos there's one thing I never
worked out, the words "Bad Wolf"

263
00:19:36,300 --> 00:19:41,100
spread across time and space,
everywhere, drawing me in,
how did you manage that?

264
00:19:41,200 --> 00:19:43,300
I did nothing.

265
00:19:43,300 --> 00:19:46,200
Oh, come on, there's no
secrets now, your worship.

266
00:19:46,200 --> 00:19:49,300
They are not part of my design.

267
00:19:51,700 --> 00:19:54,500
This is the Truth of God.

268
00:20:01,300 --> 00:20:06,700
And it's gone upmarket, this
place, they're doing little tubs of
coleslaw now. It's not very nice.

269
00:20:06,700 --> 00:20:08,900
It tastes a bit sort of clinical.

270
00:20:09,000 --> 00:20:11,900
Have you tried that new
pizza place on Minto Road?

271
00:20:11,900 --> 00:20:14,100
What's it selling? Pizza.

272
00:20:14,100 --> 00:20:16,600
That's nice. Do they deliver?

273
00:20:16,600 --> 00:20:18,200
Yeah.

274
00:20:19,700 --> 00:20:21,400
Oh, Rose, have something to eat.

275
00:20:21,500 --> 00:20:26,700
200, 000 years in the future, he's
dying, and there's nothing I can do.

276
00:20:26,700 --> 00:20:29,900
Well, like you said,
200, 000 years, it's way off.

277
00:20:30,000 --> 00:20:36,100
But it's not, it's now.
That fight is happening right now,
and he's fighting for us,

278
00:20:36,100 --> 00:20:39,700
for the whole planet, and I'm
just sitting here, eating chips!

279
00:20:39,700 --> 00:20:46,300
Listen to me, God knows,
I've hated that man, but right now
I love him and do you know why?

280
00:20:46,400 --> 00:20:51,000
Cos he did the right thing,
he sent you back to me.

281
00:20:51,000 --> 00:20:53,400
But what do I do every day, Mum?

282
00:20:53,400 --> 00:20:55,200
What do I do?

283
00:20:55,300 --> 00:21:02,000
Get up, catch the bus,
go to work, come back home,
eat chips and go to bed, is that it? !

284
00:21:02,000 --> 00:21:04,000
That's what we do. Well, I can't!

285
00:21:04,000 --> 00:21:07,000
Why? Cos you're better than us?
No, I didn't mean that!

286
00:21:10,800 --> 00:21:12,400
But it was.

287
00:21:14,100 --> 00:21:16,200
It was a better life.

288
00:21:16,300 --> 00:21:20,800
And I don't mean
all the travelling and. . .

289
00:21:20,800 --> 00:21:25,200
seeing aliens and spaceships
and things, that don't matter.

290
00:21:25,200 --> 00:21:28,500
The Doctor showed me
a better way of living your life.

291
00:21:29,700 --> 00:21:33,600
You know, he showed you, too.

292
00:21:33,700 --> 00:21:37,300
That you don't just give up,
you don't just let things happen.

293
00:21:37,400 --> 00:21:40,000
You. . .make a stand,

294
00:21:40,000 --> 00:21:41,700
you say no!

295
00:21:41,700 --> 00:21:47,000
You have the guts to do what's right
when everyone else just runs away,
and I just can't!

296
00:21:49,800 --> 00:21:55,100
Right, Lynda, you are my eyes and
ears. When the Daleks get in, follow
them on that screen and tell me.

297
00:21:55,200 --> 00:21:59,500
Yes. They'll detect you,
but the hydra combination door
should keep them out. Should?

298
00:21:59,600 --> 00:22:04,000
It's the best I can do.
How long till the fleet arrives?
'They've accelerated.'

299
00:22:08,800 --> 00:22:12,700
This is it,
ladies and gentlemen, we are at war!

300
00:22:43,300 --> 00:22:47,100
You can't spend the rest of your
life thinking about the Doctor.

301
00:22:47,100 --> 00:22:48,900
But how do I forget him?

302
00:22:48,900 --> 00:22:50,900
Start living your own life.

303
00:22:50,900 --> 00:22:56,600
A proper life,
the kind he's never had, the sort of
life that you could have with me.

304
00:23:18,200 --> 00:23:21,500
Over here. . . It's over here as well!

305
00:23:21,500 --> 00:23:24,800
That's been there for years,
it's just a phrase, just words.

306
00:23:24,900 --> 00:23:26,900
I thought it was a warning.

307
00:23:26,900 --> 00:23:28,500
Maybe it's the opposite.

308
00:23:28,500 --> 00:23:33,400
Maybe it's a message!
The same words written down now
and 200, 000 years in the future.

309
00:23:33,400 --> 00:23:37,900
It's a link between me
and the Doctor, Bad Wolf
here, Bad Wolf there.

310
00:23:38,000 --> 00:23:43,800
If it's a message, what's it saying?
It's saying I can get back! The
least I can do is help him escape!

311
00:23:44,600 --> 00:23:49,600
Stand your ground, everyone,
follow my commands and good luck.

312
00:23:52,100 --> 00:23:55,100
You were right,
they're forcing the airlock on 494.

313
00:24:12,900 --> 00:24:17,200
All the Tardis needs to do is
make a return trip. Just. . .reverse.

314
00:24:17,300 --> 00:24:22,500
But we still can't do it. The Doctor
said the Tardis is telepathic.
It's alive, it can listen.

315
00:24:22,600 --> 00:24:25,100
It's not listening now, is it?
We need to get inside it.

316
00:24:25,100 --> 00:24:28,500
Last time I saw you, with the
Slitheen, this middle bit opened,

317
00:24:28,500 --> 00:24:33,600
and there was this light, and
the Doctor said it was the heart
of the Tardis. If we can open it,

318
00:24:33,700 --> 00:24:36,200
I can make contact,
I can tell it what to do.

319
00:24:36,200 --> 00:24:39,800
Rose,
if you go back, you're gonna die.

320
00:24:39,800 --> 00:24:41,900
That's a risk I've gotta take,

321
00:24:41,900 --> 00:24:45,100
cos there's nothing left for me here.

322
00:24:45,200 --> 00:24:47,700
Nothing? No.

323
00:24:47,700 --> 00:24:52,100
OK, if that's what you think. . .
let's get this thing open.

324
00:25:05,700 --> 00:25:08,000
OK, activate internal lasers.

325
00:25:08,100 --> 00:25:10,400
Slice 'em up!

326
00:25:10,400 --> 00:25:13,800
Defences have gone off-line.
The Daleks have overridden them.

327
00:25:33,300 --> 00:25:37,200
You lied to me!
The bullets don't work!

328
00:25:55,100 --> 00:25:56,400
Faster!

329
00:26:02,500 --> 00:26:04,700
Come on!

330
00:26:04,800 --> 00:26:06,200
It's not moving!

331
00:26:21,200 --> 00:26:27,800
Advance guard have got to 495.
Jack, how are we doing?
495 should be good, I like 495.

332
00:26:29,700 --> 00:26:32,900
Identify yourself!

333
00:26:32,900 --> 00:26:34,800
You are the weakest link, goodbye!

334
00:26:37,900 --> 00:26:39,400
Yes!

335
00:26:39,500 --> 00:26:41,700
You are the weakest link!

336
00:26:44,400 --> 00:26:46,400
Goodbye. . .

337
00:26:46,400 --> 00:26:49,200
Proceed to next level.

338
00:26:51,500 --> 00:26:54,900
They're flying up the ventilation
shafts. . .No, wait a minute.

339
00:26:55,000 --> 00:26:58,700
God, why are they doing that?
They're going down!

340
00:27:06,700 --> 00:27:08,800
Exterminate!

341
00:27:08,800 --> 00:27:12,500
Exterminate! Exterminate!
Exterminate!

342
00:27:12,600 --> 00:27:14,100
Exterminate!

343
00:27:14,200 --> 00:27:16,000
Exterminate!

344
00:27:18,400 --> 00:27:20,600
You can't! You don't exist

345
00:27:21,800 --> 00:27:25,800
It's not fair! I won the game!
I should be rich!

346
00:27:25,800 --> 00:27:28,800
I'm a winner,
you can't do this to me!

347
00:27:28,800 --> 00:27:30,200
Exterminate!

348
00:27:41,800 --> 00:27:44,900
Floor Zero. . . They killed them all.

349
00:27:46,900 --> 00:27:51,300
It was never gonna work, sweetheart,
and the Doctor knew that,

350
00:27:51,300 --> 00:27:54,500
he just wanted you to be safe.
I can't give up.

351
00:27:54,500 --> 00:27:57,500
Lock the door. Walk away.

352
00:27:57,500 --> 00:27:59,000
Dad wouldn't give up.

353
00:27:59,000 --> 00:28:00,900
Well, he's not here, is he?

354
00:28:01,000 --> 00:28:04,100
And even if he was,
he'd say the same.

355
00:28:04,200 --> 00:28:08,400
No, he wouldn't.
He'd tell me to try anything.

356
00:28:08,500 --> 00:28:13,100
If I could save the Doctor's life,
try anything.

357
00:28:13,100 --> 00:28:17,700
Well, we're never gonna know.
Well, I know. Cos I met him.

358
00:28:19,000 --> 00:28:21,600
I met Dad.

359
00:28:21,600 --> 00:28:23,200
Don't be ridiculous.

360
00:28:23,300 --> 00:28:26,900
The Doctor took me back in time
and I met Dad.

361
00:28:26,900 --> 00:28:30,000
Don't say that.
Remember when Dad died?

362
00:28:30,000 --> 00:28:33,500
There was someone with him. . .

363
00:28:33,500 --> 00:28:36,600
A girl, a blonde girl.

364
00:28:36,600 --> 00:28:38,300
She held his hand.

365
00:28:41,900 --> 00:28:46,100
You saw her from a distance, Mum,
you saw her!

366
00:28:46,100 --> 00:28:47,600
Think about it!

367
00:28:47,700 --> 00:28:50,000
That was me, you saw me!

368
00:28:50,000 --> 00:28:54,800
Stop it. That's how good
the Doctor. . . Stop it! Just stop it!

369
00:29:10,500 --> 00:29:14,300
Lynda, what's happening on Earth?
The fleet's descending.

370
00:29:15,400 --> 00:29:17,300
They're bombing whole continents.

371
00:29:17,300 --> 00:29:19,500
Europa. . .

372
00:29:19,500 --> 00:29:22,600
Pacifica, the New American Alliance.

373
00:29:24,100 --> 00:29:25,600
Australasia's just. . .

374
00:29:27,200 --> 00:29:31,200
gone. This is perfection.

375
00:29:31,200 --> 00:29:34,500
I have created heaven on Earth.

376
00:29:35,700 --> 00:29:39,100
Floor 499, we're the last defence.

377
00:29:39,100 --> 00:29:42,700
The bullets should work
if you aim for the Daleks' eyestalk.

378
00:29:42,800 --> 00:29:47,700
I've got the force field at
maximum, so Dalek firepower
should be at its weakest.

379
00:29:47,800 --> 00:29:49,500
I'm only here cos of you.

380
00:29:49,500 --> 00:29:53,700
I joined the programme
cos you were on it.

381
00:29:53,800 --> 00:29:57,600
Am I supposed to say,
"When this is all over,
we could go for a drink?"

382
00:29:57,600 --> 00:30:00,800
That'd be nice. Yeah, well, tough.

383
00:30:08,600 --> 00:30:11,000
There's gotta be
something else we can do.

384
00:30:11,000 --> 00:30:13,000
Mum was right.

385
00:30:13,000 --> 00:30:16,400
Maybe we should lock the door
and walk away. I'm not having that.

386
00:30:16,400 --> 00:30:19,900
I'm not having you just. . .
give up now, no way.

387
00:30:19,900 --> 00:30:23,100
We just need something
stronger than my car,

388
00:30:24,700 --> 00:30:27,000
Something bigger,
something like that.

389
00:30:39,100 --> 00:30:44,100
You've only got this until six,
so get on with it. Where the hell
did you get that?

390
00:30:44,200 --> 00:30:49,000
Rodrigo, he owes me a favour,
never mind why, but you were right
about your dad, sweetheart.

391
00:30:49,000 --> 00:30:53,100
He was full of mad ideas, and it's
exactly what he would have done.

392
00:30:53,200 --> 00:30:56,800
Now get on with it
before I change my mind.

393
00:31:07,300 --> 00:31:10,300
Open fire!

394
00:31:30,700 --> 00:31:32,900
It's not working!

395
00:31:32,900 --> 00:31:36,200
Concentrate your fire!
Eyestalk two o'clock!

396
00:31:43,700 --> 00:31:47,600
Eye vision is impaired! I cannot see!

397
00:31:47,600 --> 00:31:49,900
We did it!

398
00:31:52,400 --> 00:31:53,800
No!

399
00:31:53,800 --> 00:31:55,900
NO!

400
00:31:55,900 --> 00:31:57,300
Aaaah!

401
00:31:59,800 --> 00:32:01,400
I've got a problem.

402
00:32:04,200 --> 00:32:07,500
Human female detected.

403
00:32:12,700 --> 00:32:17,500
They've found me. You'll be OK,
Lynda, that side's reinforced
against meteors.

404
00:32:17,500 --> 00:32:19,500
I hope so.

405
00:32:19,500 --> 00:32:21,600
You know what they say
about Earth workmanship.

406
00:33:09,800 --> 00:33:12,100
Aaaargh!

407
00:33:15,100 --> 00:33:17,600
Last man standing!

408
00:33:17,600 --> 00:33:21,900
For God's sake, Doctor,
finish that thing and kill them!

409
00:33:21,900 --> 00:33:27,500
Finish that thing and kill mankind.

410
00:33:42,400 --> 00:33:44,500
Keep going! Put your foot down!

411
00:33:48,100 --> 00:33:51,500
Faster! Give it some more, Mickey!

412
00:33:51,600 --> 00:33:52,800
Aaaah!

413
00:33:54,900 --> 00:33:56,100
Keep going!

414
00:33:57,300 --> 00:33:59,500
Come on, come on!

415
00:33:59,600 --> 00:34:02,500
Keep going! Give it some more!

416
00:34:17,000 --> 00:34:18,500
Rose!

417
00:34:37,600 --> 00:34:41,200
Doctor, you've got
20 seconds maximum!

418
00:35:15,900 --> 00:35:18,800
Exterminate!

419
00:35:18,800 --> 00:35:20,800
I kinda figured that.

420
00:35:26,200 --> 00:35:27,700
It's ready!

421
00:35:41,600 --> 00:35:44,200
You really wanna think about this.

422
00:35:44,300 --> 00:35:48,400
Cos if I activate the signal,
every living creature dies.

423
00:35:48,500 --> 00:35:51,000
I am immortal.

424
00:35:51,000 --> 00:35:56,900
Do you wanna put that to the test?
I want to see you become like me.

425
00:35:56,900 --> 00:36:02,000
Hail the Doctor,
the Great Exterminator!

426
00:36:02,100 --> 00:36:05,800
I'll do it!
Then prove yourself, Doctor!

427
00:36:05,800 --> 00:36:09,400
What are you - coward or killer?

428
00:36:19,300 --> 00:36:21,500
Coward.

429
00:36:21,500 --> 00:36:23,200
Any day.

430
00:36:23,200 --> 00:36:28,800
Mankind will be harvested
because of YOUR weakness.

431
00:36:28,800 --> 00:36:31,200
And what about me?

432
00:36:31,300 --> 00:36:33,200
Am I becoming one of your angels?

433
00:36:33,200 --> 00:36:36,000
You are the Heathen.

434
00:36:36,000 --> 00:36:40,300
You will be exterminated.

435
00:36:40,400 --> 00:36:43,000
Maybe it's time.

436
00:36:52,300 --> 00:36:55,000
Alert! Tardis materialising!

437
00:36:55,100 --> 00:36:57,900
You will not escape!

438
00:37:09,300 --> 00:37:11,300
What have you done? !

439
00:37:11,300 --> 00:37:14,300
I looked into the Tardis,

440
00:37:14,300 --> 00:37:16,400
and the Tardis looked into me.

441
00:37:16,400 --> 00:37:18,400
You looked into the time vortex.

442
00:37:18,500 --> 00:37:20,400
Rose, no-one's meant to see that.

443
00:37:20,500 --> 00:37:23,500
This is the Abomination!

444
00:37:23,600 --> 00:37:25,400
Exterminate!

445
00:37:31,300 --> 00:37:33,500
I am the Bad Wolf.

446
00:37:33,600 --> 00:37:35,600
I create myself.

447
00:37:38,300 --> 00:37:40,500
I take the words. . .

448
00:37:42,000 --> 00:37:45,500
I scatter them in time and space.

449
00:37:47,500 --> 00:37:50,400
A message to lead myself here.

450
00:37:50,500 --> 00:37:55,200
Rose, you've got to stop this,
you've got to stop this now!

451
00:37:56,900 --> 00:38:01,000
You've got the entire vortex running
through your head, you'll burn!

452
00:38:01,000 --> 00:38:03,500
I want you safe.

453
00:38:04,700 --> 00:38:06,500
My Doctor. . .

454
00:38:06,600 --> 00:38:09,600
protected from the false god.

455
00:38:09,700 --> 00:38:14,300
You cannot hurt me! I am immortal!

456
00:38:14,300 --> 00:38:17,300
You are tiny.

457
00:38:17,300 --> 00:38:20,500
I can see the whole
of time and space,

458
00:38:20,600 --> 00:38:24,800
every single atom of your existence,
and I divide them.

459
00:38:30,100 --> 00:38:32,800
Everything must come to dust.

460
00:38:35,800 --> 00:38:37,700
All things.

461
00:38:37,700 --> 00:38:40,100
Everything dies.

462
00:38:46,900 --> 00:38:48,700
The Time War ends.

463
00:38:48,800 --> 00:38:51,400
I will not die!

464
00:38:52,900 --> 00:38:57,200
I cannot di-i-i-ie!

465
00:39:12,800 --> 00:39:14,800
Rose, you've done it, now stop.

466
00:39:16,300 --> 00:39:21,300
Just let go.
How can I let go of this?

467
00:39:22,300 --> 00:39:24,200
I bring life.

468
00:39:25,800 --> 00:39:29,800
But this is wrong!
You can't control life and death!

469
00:39:29,900 --> 00:39:31,300
But I can.

470
00:39:32,300 --> 00:39:35,700
The sun and the moon,

471
00:39:35,700 --> 00:39:37,500
the day and night.

472
00:39:38,700 --> 00:39:40,600
But why do they hurt?

473
00:39:40,600 --> 00:39:43,300
The power's gonna kill you,
and it's my fault!

474
00:39:43,400 --> 00:39:46,800
I can see everything. . .

475
00:39:47,700 --> 00:39:50,000
All that is. . .

476
00:39:50,100 --> 00:39:52,700
all that was. . .

477
00:39:52,800 --> 00:39:55,300
all that ever could be.

478
00:39:57,200 --> 00:40:00,500
That's what I see, all the time.

479
00:40:00,500 --> 00:40:02,600
And doesn't it drive you mad?

480
00:40:02,600 --> 00:40:05,000
My head. . .

481
00:40:05,000 --> 00:40:06,200
Come here.

482
00:40:06,300 --> 00:40:08,300
It's killing me.

483
00:40:08,300 --> 00:40:10,600
I think you need a doctor.

484
00:41:54,100 --> 00:41:55,900
What happened?

485
00:41:55,900 --> 00:41:57,400
Don't you remember?

486
00:41:59,300 --> 00:42:03,600
It's like. . .there was this singing.

487
00:42:03,600 --> 00:42:06,600
That's right, I sang a song
and the Daleks ran away!

488
00:42:06,600 --> 00:42:08,600
I was at home.

489
00:42:08,700 --> 00:42:12,400
No, I wasn't,
I was in the Tardis and. . .

490
00:42:12,400 --> 00:42:14,900
there was this light.

491
00:42:15,900 --> 00:42:18,400
I can't remember anything else.

492
00:42:23,800 --> 00:42:26,500
Rose Tyler!

493
00:42:26,600 --> 00:42:30,300
I was gonna take you
to so many places, Barcelona.

494
00:42:30,300 --> 00:42:35,200
Not the city Barcelona,
the planet Barcelona, you'd love it,
fantastic place!

495
00:42:35,200 --> 00:42:38,200
They've got dogs with no noses!

496
00:42:38,200 --> 00:42:42,200
Imagine how many times you'd tell
that joke and it's still funny!

497
00:42:42,300 --> 00:42:48,200
Then why can't we go?
Maybe you will, and maybe I will,
but not like this.

498
00:42:48,200 --> 00:42:50,000
You're not making sense.

499
00:42:50,000 --> 00:42:54,200
I might never make sense again,
I might have two heads or no head!

500
00:42:54,200 --> 00:42:57,400
Imagine me with no head,
and don't say that's an improvement.

501
00:42:57,400 --> 00:43:02,700
But it's a bit dodgy,
this process. You never know
what you'll end up with!

502
00:43:03,500 --> 00:43:06,400
Doctor! Stay away!

503
00:43:07,300 --> 00:43:09,100
Tell me what's goin' on.

504
00:43:09,100 --> 00:43:13,200
I absorbed all the energy
of the time vortex,
and no-one's meant to do that.

505
00:43:17,400 --> 00:43:19,200
Every cell in my body's dying.

506
00:43:19,300 --> 00:43:23,700
Well, can't you do something?
Yeah, I'm doin' it now!

507
00:43:23,800 --> 00:43:29,500
Time Lords have this little trick.
it's, er. . .sort of a way
of cheating death.

508
00:43:31,200 --> 00:43:32,800
Except. . .

509
00:43:34,600 --> 00:43:36,900
.it means I'm gonna change.

510
00:43:39,000 --> 00:43:40,600
I'm not gonna see you again. . .

511
00:43:42,200 --> 00:43:45,700
.not like this,
not with this daft old face.

512
00:43:47,500 --> 00:43:49,600
And before I go. . . Don't say that!

513
00:43:49,700 --> 00:43:51,800
Rose. . .

514
00:43:51,800 --> 00:43:56,100
before I go, I just wanna tell you,
you were fantastic.

515
00:43:57,900 --> 00:44:00,600
Absolutely fantastic!

516
00:44:02,400 --> 00:44:04,300
And do you know what?

517
00:44:07,400 --> 00:44:09,400
So was I!

518
00:44:29,500 --> 00:44:31,800
Hello! OK. . .

519
00:44:34,500 --> 00:44:37,300
New teeth, that's weird.
Where was I?

520
00:44:37,400 --> 00:44:41,400
Oh, that's right! Barcelona!

521
00:45:06,000 --> 00:45:11,900
